Subject: the notification area draws its icons at 16 px, and keeps one row

The owner's ask of 2026-11-04 is a notification area like Windows 11's:
small icons, one row. Measured first, because the plan said nothing about
where the size comes from.

🚨 Measured on 2026-11-06, against this source:

    applets/systemtray/qml/main.qml:185
        readonly property int smallIconSize: Kirigami.Units.iconSizes.smallMedium
    applets/systemtray/qml/main.qml:193
        rowsOrColumns: ... Math.floor(gridThickness / (smallIconSize + smallSpacing))
    applets/systemtray/main.xml:33
        "tray icons will be capped at the smallMedium size (22px)"

and the numbers themselves, read out of the real Kirigami 6.13.0 on this
machine rather than assumed (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen qml6):

    iconSizes.small = 16   iconSizes.smallMedium = 22   smallSpacing = 4
    roundedIconSize(16) = 16

So today a tray icon is drawn at 22 logical units whenever the panel is not
auto-scaling, which is the default (scaleIconsToFit defaults to false). That
is the whole of the measurement: one property, one place.

🚨 And the one-word change is wrong, which is the reason this patch is four
files and not one line. The SAME property is the divisor that decides how
many rows of icons the panel holds, so pointing it at iconSizes.small
changes the row count too -- on the 48 px panel Raye itself ships
(layout.js, patches/plasma-desktop/0003):

    floor(48 / (22 + 4)) = 1 row      <- today, and what is wanted
    floor(48 / (16 + 4)) = 2 rows     <- what smallIconSize: small gives

Two rows of tray icons on Raye's own panel is the opposite of the look
asked for, it reads as unfinished, and nothing would have said so: both
numbers are valid, the applet loads, and the only evidence is on a screen.
It is the same shape this tree has paid for repeatedly -- a value written
where something else also reads it -- and this time it was caught by doing
the arithmetic before the edit rather than after.

The two therefore come apart, in a file of their own: the icon is
iconSizes.small, the row divisor stays at iconSizes.smallMedium +
smallSpacing, which is what it already was. Upstream's stated intent is
preserved exactly along with it -- "Should change to 2 rows/columns on a
56px panel" is still floor(56 / 26) = 2 -- so this patch changes the size
of an icon and nothing else about the layout. root.oneRowOrColumn, which
other parts of the applet read, keeps the value it has today.

⚠️ Two traps that were checked rather than reasoned about.

  * The size is NOT a pixel literal. Kirigami.Units.iconSizes scales with
    the font and the device pixel ratio (IconSizes::iconScaleFactor, in
    Kirigami/Platform/Units), so a high-density screen is handed 16
    logical units and not 16 physical dots. A hard-coded 16 would have
    been a bug on exactly the screens that notice.
  * 16 is a size the icon themes really ship, so nothing is resampled and
    nothing turns blurry: Raye's own theme has status/16 with real SVGs
    (theme/icons/Raye-Dark), it inherits breeze-dark which ships /16 too,
    and Kirigami's own roundedIconSize(16) is 16 -- it does not round the
    request away to another size.

⚠️ The new QML file is listed in plasma_add_applet(QML_SOURCES), and that
is not housekeeping. The applet's QML is compiled into a module from an
explicit list, so a file left out of it does not exist at runtime and the
component fails to resolve -- the applet would not load at all. The test
asserts the listing for that reason, because the failure is only visible in
a session.

⚠️ What this patch does NOT claim. It changes the size the applet asks for.
It does not measure what the notification area looks like, because that
needs a Plasma session and there is none on the machine this was written
on. What is measured is the number, where it comes from, what it does to
the row count, and that the theme can supply it.

main.xml's label for scaleIconsToFit is updated with it: it is the only
place in the source that writes the cap down, and leaving it saying 22px
would leave a false statement next to the code it describes. It is not a
string the configuration UI shows -- ConfigGeneral.qml has its own i18nc
strings for the "Panel icon size" combobox -- so no translation regresses.
That combobox's "Small" option now means what it says.

Reason: this cannot be done outside the source. The size is a QML binding
inside the system tray applet's compiled QML module; there is no
configuration key for it, and the only key in the neighbourhood,
scaleIconsToFit, does the opposite -- it abandons the fixed size and scales
icons to the panel's thickness. A look-and-feel package cannot reach it
either: the applet's QML is shipped by plasma-workspace, not by a theme,
and the one mechanism that could override a file of it is a dpkg-divert,
which this repository is explicitly moving away from. Splitting the icon
size from the row divisor is a change of structure in that QML, which no
setting of any kind can express.

